{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Balanced binary search trees as sorted sets and sorted dictionaries."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/binarysearchtrees"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"title":"BinarySearchTrees","symbolKind":"module","externalID":"BinarySearchTrees","modules":[{"name":"BinarySearchTrees"}],"role":"collection","roleHeading":"Framework"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sorted-sets","identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/AVLTree","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/RedBlackTree","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap"],"title":"Sorted sets"},{"anchor":"Sorted-dictionaries","identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/AVLDictionary"],"title":"Sorted dictionaries"},{"anchor":"Extended-Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Trees"],"generated":true,"title":"Extended Modules"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/AVLTree"},{"type":"text","text":" is a sorted set and an "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/AVLDictionary"},{"type":"text","text":" a sorted dictionary, both kept in an AVL"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tree (Adelson-Velsky and Landis, 1962): the heights of every vertex’s subtrees differ by at most"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one, so lookup, insertion and removal take O(log "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":") and the height stays below"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"1.4405 log₂("},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" + 2) − 0.3277. A "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/RedBlackTree"},{"type":"text","text":" is the same sorted set kept in a red–black"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tree (Guibas and Sedgewick, 1978), whose height stays at most 2 log₂("},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" + 1) and whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"insertions and removals rotate at most two and three times. A "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap"},{"type":"text","text":" (Seidel and Aragon,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"1996) keeps a random priority on each vertex, so its shape is a random binary search tree’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whatever order the elements came in: O(log "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":") expected for each operation, plus "},{"code":"split(at:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and "},{"code":"join(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which cut a set at an element and put two sets that don’t interleave back"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"together. The sets share one API, so any of them can stand in for another. Their elements are random-access collections in ascending order,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indexed by rank, with "},{"code":"lowerBound(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"upperBound(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"elements(in:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for range queries."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import BinarySearchTrees","","var primes: AVLTree = [7, 2, 11, 3, 5]","primes.insert(13)","primes.contains(4)      \/\/ false","primes.lowerBound(6)    \/\/ 3, the index of 7","","var stock: AVLDictionary = [\"pear\": 4, \"apple\": 7]","stock[\"fig\"] = 2","stock.map(\\.key)        \/\/ [\"apple\", \"fig\", \"pear\"]"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertices live in flat arrays linked by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int32"},{"type":"text","text":" slots, so a tree is a copy-on-write value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that copies a few arrays, and only when a shared copy is mutated. Its shape converts to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Grafluent’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryTree"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryTree(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (import Grafluent’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trees"},{"type":"text","text":" module beside this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one), so Grafluent’s tree algorithms and drawings run over it."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://BinarySearchTrees/documentation/BinarySearchTrees/Trees":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Trees","abstract":[],"title":"Trees","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/binarysearchtrees\/trees","role":"collection","kind":"symbol"},"doc://BinarySearchTrees/documentation/BinarySearchTrees/AVLDictionary":{"url":"\/documentation\/binarysearchtrees\/avldictionary","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/AVLDictionary","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A sorted dictionary kept in an AVL tree: unique keys in ascending order, each with a value."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AVLDictionary"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AVLDictionary"}],"title":"AVLDictionary"},"doc://BinarySearchTrees/documentation/BinarySearchTrees":{"url":"\/documentation\/binarysearchtrees","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Balanced binary search trees as sorted sets and sorted dictionaries."}],"role":"collection","title":"BinarySearchTrees"},"doc://BinarySearchTrees/documentation/BinarySearchTrees/AVLTree":{"url":"\/documentation\/binarysearchtrees\/avltree","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/AVLTree","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A sorted set kept in an AVL tree: a binary search tree in which the heights of every vertex’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"two subtrees differ by at most one (Adelson-Velsky and Landis, 1962)."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AVLTree","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AVLTree","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"AVLTree"},"doc://BinarySearchTrees/documentation/BinarySearchTrees/Treap":{"url":"\/documentation\/binarysearchtrees\/treap","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A sorted set kept in a treap: a binary search tree whose vertices also carry random"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"priorities, with no vertex of higher priority than its parent (Seidel and Aragon, 1996)."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Treap","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Treap","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Treap"},"doc://BinarySearchTrees/documentation/BinarySearchTrees/RedBlackTree":{"kind":"symbol","title":"RedBlackTree","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RedBlackTree","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A sorted set kept in a red–black tree: a binary search tree whose vertices are red or black,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with no red vertex under a red one and the same number of black vertices on every path from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"root down (Guibas and Sedgewick, 1978)."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RedBlackTree","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/binarysearchtrees\/redblacktree","identifier":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/RedBlackTree"}}}